  "boundaries": [
    "The optional method requests identity encoding by default, preserves explicit caller negotiation, validates the routed dataset before HTTP, and consumes the response body once through the existing TLS/allowlist/timeout/circuit/concurrency/cleanup path.",
    "Request and response scopes are caller declarations. The method returns parsed payload plus BATCH SHA, byte count and EOF UTC; raw body bytes are not retained in this DTO or persisted.",
    "The agent's initial 65 tests precede the identity-header change; final root 90 tests include those scenarios. These are repeated and expanded runs, not 155 unique scenarios.",
    "The expected red failure is the missing default Accept-Encoding; no independent red stdout/stderr files were retained or fabricated.",
    "No provider, Application, RawAudit, FinancialFact or policy3 adopts this method yet; no historical announcement/availability/native-row-ID repair, PostgreSQL test, VPS deployment or production acceptance is claimed."
